+/// Capability `recipe-types`, server mods only (manifest `api = "0.3"`,
+/// experimental): the recipes of types the mod brings. A recipe file
+/// `data/<namespace>/recipe/<path>.json` whose `type` is outside `minecraft`
+/// is kept as it is written; the mod reads it as it likes, and asks the game
+/// which items an ingredient of it names (the game knows the item tags).
+interface recipe-types {
+    record custom-recipe {
+        /// `<namespace>:<path>`, its place under `data/<namespace>/recipe/`.
+        id: string,
+        /// The file's JSON.
+        json: string,
+    }
+    /// The recipes of type `kind` (`mymod:crushing`), in file order, from the
+    /// content mods and the world's data packs. Empty for a type nobody uses.
+    recipes-of-type: func(kind: string) -> list<custom-recipe>;
+    /// The items an ingredient names, in order, once each: `ingredient` is
+    /// JSON, an item id, a `#tag`, a list of them, or an object with an
+    /// `item`, a `tag` or `items`. A bare id is `minecraft:`; items the game
+    /// doesn't know are left out.
+    ingredient-items: func(ingredient: string) -> list<string>;
+}
+
